cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to MemoryFence, please cite it using the metadata below.
  MemoryFence is in its research-design phase and has not produced experimental results.
type: software
title: "MemoryFence: A Research Framework for Evaluating Persistent Memory Poisoning, Provenance, and Deletion Security in Collaborative AI Agents"
abstract: >-
  MemoryFence is a research framework, currently in design, for measuring under what
  conditions attacker-origin instructions persist in derived AI memories after transformations
  or original-source deletion, and how deletion handling, provenance completeness, and defense
  mechanisms influence unauthorized downstream agent behavior in collaborative AI agents.
authors:
  - given-names: Yug Amol
    family-names: More
    alias: Yug-More
version: 0.1.0.dev0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yug-More/memoryfence"
keywords:
  - AI security
  - LLM agents
  - memory poisoning
  - prompt injection
  - provenance
  - machine unlearning
  - access control
